Conserve stable argument paths in dependent-application rechecking

Rechecking a dependent application substituted the capture-adapted rechecked
argument type into later formals; box adaptation can widen a stable argument's
singleton type, and substituting the widened type turns a later formal's
`x.Result` selection into a type projection that the actual argument no longer
conforms to. A method whose using evidence selects a member of an earlier
using parameter through a doubly-nested refining alias (Soundness's
`value is Multiplicable by value` with `multiplicable.Result =:= value`,
issue #1411) fails at every non-inline call site under capture checking —
including the synthesized export forwarders of the soundness package.
Substituting the argument's stable path (as the typer did) mirrors the
singleton conservation recheckApplication#instArgs already performs for
dependent result types.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude); 8-line reproduction in the feature
documentation.

The same conservation is applied on the result side: recheckApplication's
instArgs previously conserved stable paths only for unboxed capturing
rechecked types, so a stable argument widened to a plain non-capturing type
still turned a dependent result's member selection into a projection.

Proscala-Patch: dependarg
